I have been following your posts on rearing sauropod mounts, and I guess you missed the rearing Uberabatitan from Brazil.

This photo is not mine.

The exhibition is located at the Centro de Pesquisa Paleontológica Lewellyn Ivor Price (CPPLIP), which has its own museum, labs, and in situ excavation sites at the Serra da Galga Formation (Bauru Group). It is located in rural Peirópolis, on farms near Uberaba, Minas Gerais. The CPPLIP is a public institution affiliated with UFTM.

I do not have a photo of my own to share, but please ask my friend Prof Thiago Marinho for one for your paper. He collaborates as a curator there. 

thiago.marinho@uftm.edu.br and tsmarinho@gmail.com

--

Centro de Pesquisas Paleontológicas Llewellyn Ivor Price (CPPLIP)
at Universidade Federal do Triângulo Mineiro or UFTM) (Federal University of Triângulo Mineiro)
in Peiropolis, near the city of Uberaba, Minas Gerais, Brazil
